{"title":"2021 USAJMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/36267c5f4ee67ae71ac26988998233a17818f69b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Note:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> For any geometry problem whose statement begins with an asterisk <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d02e715e7f7195675151570530c5b62ba7b2744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, the first page of the solution must be a large, in-scale, clearly labeled diagram. Failure to meet this requirement will result in an automatic 1-point deduction.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e6cd0e4103015efba12e0fc4291f012b467eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> denote the set of positive integers. Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f84ba5284b311a66dd04f32ff5f63dd497acf765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : \\mathbb{N} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> such that for positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1d6265e67657b5886ce257671d45ff9c0282eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"12\" height=\"16\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/f/c1f8ffe04cfcc45b498f3931a4796d5c56dc04d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(a^2 + b^2) = f(a)f(b) \\text{ and } f(a^2) = f(a)^2.\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Rectangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/b/29b16bf008f507f2c3876bc743f9058ecb7b5af7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCC_1B_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/6/f1622e15f29040cc3d0ad7e9aab99fe6e983e759.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CAA_1C_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cd1d5a14692916a1824c952e77a5d3d2d82e499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABB_1A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" /> are erected outside an acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd222166def59a3315433877917a826de6488031.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> Suppose that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/376bddb409086c44748da5c8fdb4271e2122f695.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BC_1C+\\angle  CA_1A+\\angle AB_1B=180^{\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"293\" height=\"16\" />Prove that lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df5b6d99e91936a974c9f93bfe2bd3b9f6b8156b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1C_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/b/10b85bab40fe89e79163c476adadb6b5604706ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1A_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1dbd68bf0453f67a0e5ff57ccf9a818a835788a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1B_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> are concurrent.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>An equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a737670d481129e2ead6d7223437f3cf70ea53f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/0/770fcb6144b56caa2e6b9574dc1a13c0d1353bd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> is given. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> equilateral triangles with side length 1 and with non-overlapping interiors are drawn inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a737670d481129e2ead6d7223437f3cf70ea53f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, such that each unit equilateral triangle has sides parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a737670d481129e2ead6d7223437f3cf70ea53f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, but with opposite orientation. (An example with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is drawn below.)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab00fe73ccc6121244ce7f6bbd5f89bced7f2d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1/2,sqrt(3)/2)--cycle,linewidth(0.5)); filldraw((0.45,0.55)--(0.65,0.55)--(0.55,0.55-sqrt(3)/2*0.2)--cycle,gray,linewidth(0.5)); filldraw((0.54,0.3)--(0.34,0.3)--(0.44,0.3-sqrt(3)/2*0.2)--cycle,gray,linewidth(0.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"218\" />\nProve that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95fe9c1b574a4e693e5ad5190a56fcb62aa26701.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n \\leq \\frac{2}{3} L^{2}.\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Carina has three pins, labeled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, located at the origin of the coordinate plane. In a move, Carina may move a pin to an adjacent lattice point at distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> away. What is the least number of moves that Carina can make in order for triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> to have area 2021? \n</p><p>(A lattice point is a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> in the coordinate plane where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are both integers, not necessarily positive.) \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A finite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of positive integers has the property that, for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16fc20504e4578a5cb8595270381f8a6cd9e0e8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\in S,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> and each positive integer divisor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, there exists a unique element <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cf6d4461b12bd13210f943324486ca9ea7c1a05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/3116192db5ce09fcdf089120742d4b7df9a34b8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{gcd}(s, t) = d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />. (The elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> could be equal.) Given this information, find all possible values for the number of elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/83870118206bd0e612b5c9e3def2ef95460e368b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an integer. Find all positive real solutions to the following system of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> equations: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301cd0ead59d39f1135e7e94925f2eeda12023c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a_{1} &amp;=\\frac{1}{a_{2 n}}+\\frac{1}{a_{2}}, &amp; a_{2}&amp;=a_{1}+a_{3}, \\\\ a_{3}&amp;=\\frac{1}{a_{2}}+\\frac{1}{a_{4}}, &amp; a_{4}&amp;=a_{3}+a_{5}, \\\\ a_{5}&amp;=\\frac{1}{a_{4}}+\\frac{1}{a_{6}}, &amp; a_{6}&amp;=a_{5}+a_{7}, \\\\ &amp;\\vdots \\\\ a_{2 n-1}&amp;=\\frac{1}{a_{2 n-2}}+\\frac{1}{a_{2 n}}, &amp; a_{2 n}&amp;=a_{2 n-1}+a_{1} \\end{align*}\" width=\"357\" height=\"217\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO\" title=\"2021 USAJMO\">2021 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2021\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems\" title=\"2020 USOJMO Problems\">2020 USOJMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2022 USAJMO Problems\">2022 USAJMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018044636\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 260/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1286/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 84/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7963/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.130      1 -total\n 61.27%   10.495      1 Template:USAJMO_box\n 37.36%    6.400      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21093:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018044636 and revision id 196459. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}